# An allowlist, not a denylist: everything at the root is ignored unless named
# below. `vercel deploy` uploads this folder and does NOT read .gitignore, so a
# denylist that forgot one entry would upload it. What is at stake if it did:
#   .env          every secret the server and app use
#   .expo/        the dev log, which holds the .env values in plain text
#   /data/        the Supabase export: real weight and meal history (POPIA)
#   .scratch/     session handoffs
# Only the inputs to `npm run build:server` travel. A new top-level folder the
# server needs must be added here, or the build fails loudly; that is the
# intended failure, not a silent upload.
/*
!server
!packages
!package.json
!package-lock.json
!tsconfig.json
!vercel.json

# Re-ignored inside the allowed folders, so an env file added under server/ or
# packages/ later still never uploads. Deliberately NOT `**/data/`: that would
# also drop server/data/, the scoped query layer (see the /data/ note in
# .gitignore for the time an unanchored `data` rule did exactly that).
**/.env*
